1
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:11,040
I came to ask for your kindness, Grandpa.

2
00:03:11,120 --> 00:03:13,160
PREVIOUSLY

3
00:03:13,240 --> 00:03:16,520
<i>The villagers are in trouble.
I think you can help them, Grandpa.</i>

4
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:20,760
Hathaya stole the spotlight
and grabbed all his attention.

5
00:03:20,840 --> 00:03:21,680
I hate her.

6
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:25,280
She came back here
to steal our inheritance.

7
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,720
<i>I won't let her take what belongs to me.</i>

8
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:30,960
I want to know who Hathaya's mother

9
00:03:31,040 --> 00:03:33,880
<i>is living with and what she does</i>

10
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:35,880
<i>and whether Hathaya's grandmother
is really sick.</i>

11
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:38,120
Is your granddaughter not here?

12
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:39,440
It's a long story.

13
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:42,960
If there's anything
you want to tell me, I'm listening.

14
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:55,280
Hey!

15
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:56,960
Why are you setting those off?

16
00:03:57,480 --> 00:04:00,160
If something happens to her,
you're going to jail!

17
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:01,360
Where's your daughter?

18
00:04:01,440 --> 00:04:04,080
Hathai took the money to pay you.

19
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:05,600
If she paid her debt,

20
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:07,360
I wouldn't even be here!

21
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:10,800
She left with the money yesterday.
She still hasn't come back.

22
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:12,840
You people are trying to mess with us?

23
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:16,560
DUANGJAI'S FOOD STALL

24
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:17,959
Don't!

25
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:20,880
Those are the things
I use to make a living! Stop!

26
00:04:21,519 --> 00:04:24,200
This is going too far.
I'm calling the police.

27
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:40,280
Eggs! Grilled eggs here!

28
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:43,080
Grilled eggs!

29
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:47,920
You! Get over here!

30
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:51,640
If you run, I'll kill you!

31
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:53,760
If I don't run, I'll die anyway!

32
00:04:58,880 --> 00:05:00,080
After her!

33
00:05:01,280 --> 00:05:02,720
Please help Hathai!

34
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:05,320
They're going to kill her!
Please help her!

35
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:08,480
- Please help!
- Yes.

36
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:09,680
Alright?

37
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:11,880
Oh, Hathai.

38
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:27,240
Those bastards! They nearly killed me!

39
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:34,160
Damn it. Thought you were so tough, huh?

40
00:05:34,240 --> 00:05:35,280
You losers!

41
00:05:35,360 --> 00:05:36,720
Who are you calling losers?

42
00:05:44,840 --> 00:05:47,280
I wasn't talking about you.

43
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:48,200
I meant myself.

44
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:50,200
I warned you.

45
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:51,840
No money,

46
00:05:51,920 --> 00:05:53,880
you die.

47
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:56,120
Come on.

48
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:12,120
Let's go!

49
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:17,640
Ma'am, you're safe--

50
00:06:22,280 --> 00:06:23,760
I survived!

51
00:06:23,840 --> 00:06:25,640
Mom! Mom! Help me!

52
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:27,240
I'm back, Mom!

53
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:29,200
Mom!

54
00:06:29,280 --> 00:06:31,440
How can you be this awful?!

55
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:34,280
You really are terrible!

56
00:06:34,360 --> 00:06:36,120
Why didn't you use the money
to pay them back?

57
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:37,960
Where is the money?
What did you do with it?

58
00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:42,600
Oh, Mom! I gambled all of it away.

59
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:45,520
I thought I'd win one or two million,

60
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:49,160
but I lost everything.

61
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:51,640
How could you do this?!

62
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:53,880
Mom! Come on, Mom!

63
00:06:53,960 --> 00:06:55,320
I did it because

64
00:06:55,400 --> 00:06:57,800
I wanted money for your treatment.

65
00:06:58,400 --> 00:07:00,160
I don't want you to have to work anymore.

66
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:02,520
And I want Hathaya
to come back and live with us.

67
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:04,440
I did it for us, Mom.

68
00:07:04,520 --> 00:07:06,240
I love you and my daughter.

69
00:07:06,320 --> 00:07:08,440
If you really loved me and your daughter,

70
00:07:08,520 --> 00:07:10,760
you wouldn't keep doing
stupid things like this.

71
00:07:10,840 --> 00:07:12,800
All you do is cause problems.

72
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:15,400
I don't know what to do with you anymore.

73
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:19,120
Mom! I know I was wrong.

74
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:21,040
I'm sorry.

75
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:27,480
And now there's no money
left to pay the debt.

76
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:28,960
What are we going to do now?

77
00:07:38,640 --> 00:07:39,560
Mom.

78
00:07:41,160 --> 00:07:42,320
Call Hathaya.

79
00:07:42,400 --> 00:07:45,200
Tell her you've been hospitalized
and need emergency surgery.

80
00:07:46,080 --> 00:07:48,080
Tell her to send money.

81
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:51,160
Then I'll use that money
to pay those people.

82
00:07:51,240 --> 00:07:53,200
Please, Mom. Call her now.

83
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:54,520
Hathaya listens to you.

84
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:58,000
If she doesn't have the money,
she'll find a way to get it somehow.

85
00:07:58,080 --> 00:07:59,600
She's a devoted granddaughter, Mom.

86
00:07:59,680 --> 00:08:03,040
Trust me. Come on. Call her.

87
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:05,720
Call her, Mom.

88
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,080
Mom!

89
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:11,680
When are you going to stop
being so selfish?

90
00:08:11,760 --> 00:08:13,800
All you ever think about is yourself.

91
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:16,040
Huh? You lie

92
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:18,800
and stir up trouble
just to save your own skin.

93
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:21,880
I feel so sorry for Hathaya

94
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:23,560
for being born as your daughter.

95
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:27,760
She's my daughter.
She's supposed to help me.

96
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:32,159
If you won't call her,
I will call her myself.

97
00:08:33,679 --> 00:08:37,080
And if she refuses to help me,
I'll disown her.

98
00:08:37,840 --> 00:08:41,679
Oh, Mom! You broke the phone!

99
00:08:41,760 --> 00:08:42,799
Good!

100
00:08:43,320 --> 00:08:44,720
- Then give me yours.
- No.

101
00:08:44,800 --> 00:08:47,120
- Where is it?
- I won't give it to you.

102
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:49,960
- Let go of me. I won't give it to you.
- Where's your phone?

103
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:52,360
- Stay away from me.
- I'll call Hathaya.

104
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:54,160
They're back!

105
00:08:54,240 --> 00:08:55,760
They're coming back!

106
00:08:58,320 --> 00:08:59,640
I'm out.

107
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:02,080
Hathai!

108
00:09:05,840 --> 00:09:07,000
Grandma.

109
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:10,160
You need to run too.

110
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:11,680
Hurry!

111
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:14,640
Grandma, they're already gone.

112
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:17,440
I lied so your daughter would run away.

113
00:09:29,640 --> 00:09:30,880
Grandpa.

114
00:09:36,920 --> 00:09:39,400
Thank you so much

115
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:40,720
for giving them a chance.

116
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:46,320
You asked me why

117
00:09:46,840 --> 00:09:49,840
I was willing to risk my future

118
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:53,600
on people who aren't my relatives
or even people I know.

119
00:09:55,280 --> 00:09:57,720
It's because I've always remembered
what you taught me.

120
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:04,520
When I was little, you told me

121
00:10:05,320 --> 00:10:07,760
that you started with nothing,

122
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:10,160
but you were lucky

123
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:13,320
because someone gave you a chance to work.

124
00:10:14,760 --> 00:10:16,800
That opportunity let you build a life.

125
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:21,000
And the housing developments you created

126
00:10:21,080 --> 00:10:23,800
have given opportunities
to many other people too.

127
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:33,480
That's only part of the reason
I agreed to let them stay here.

128
00:10:35,160 --> 00:10:36,600
The main reason I was interested

129
00:10:37,960 --> 00:10:41,280
was your wager.

130
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:49,000
Remember what you said.
If any problem comes up,

131
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:51,840
you have to leave this house

132
00:10:52,760 --> 00:10:55,360
and never set foot here again
for the rest of your life.

133
00:10:56,600 --> 00:10:57,800
Yes.

134
00:11:18,960 --> 00:11:19,800
HATHAYA

135
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:29,440
Hathaya, sweetheart?

136
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:33,840
Yes, it's your beautiful Hathaya.

137
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:35,520
<i>How are you, Grandma?</i>

138
00:11:36,440 --> 00:11:38,080
I'm fine, sweetheart.

139
00:11:38,680 --> 00:11:41,880
Grandma, I did something good today.

140
00:11:41,960 --> 00:11:44,320
I helped some villagers facing demolition.

141
00:11:44,400 --> 00:11:48,160
Then I asked Grandpa to hire them
to work at the site,

142
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:50,120
and Grandpa agreed.

143
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:52,760
Your grandpa is a good man.

144
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:56,080
You need to love him
and take good care of him.

145
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:59,840
I will, Grandma. I'll do my best.

146
00:12:00,560 --> 00:12:03,120
Grandma, how is Mom?

147
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:14,600
Grandma? What's wrong?

148
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:16,000
Why are you crying?

149
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:20,120
I'm just overwhelmed, sweetheart.

150
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:23,880
I'm proud that my granddaughter
is a good person who helps others.

151
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:31,160
Grandma, Mom paid off
the debt already, right?

152
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:39,160
Your mother paid it all off.
You don't need to worry.

153
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:43,480
Just focus on your work. And remember

154
00:12:43,560 --> 00:12:45,640
<i>to be grateful to the people who help you.</i>

155
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:48,520
Okay, Grandma.

156
00:12:49,040 --> 00:12:53,000
I love you more than anyone in the world.

157
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:55,880
I'm going to bed now.

158
00:12:56,560 --> 00:12:58,600
Okay. Kisses.

159
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:00,520
Okay, sweetheart.

160
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:28,040
Grandma,

161
00:13:30,040 --> 00:13:32,480
why didn't you just tell her the truth?

162
00:13:33,680 --> 00:13:36,160
Hathaya has suffered enough already.

163
00:13:36,240 --> 00:13:40,160
I don't want my granddaughter
to worry any more than she already does.

164
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:46,920
Grandmother and granddaughter
are exactly alike.

165
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:49,360
You know my granddaughter, don't you?

166
00:13:52,920 --> 00:13:55,880
No. So...

167
00:13:57,320 --> 00:13:59,200
What are you going to do now?

168
00:14:01,120 --> 00:14:03,600
Whatever can still be used,
I'll keep using.

169
00:14:04,280 --> 00:14:05,920
Then I'll borrow some money

170
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:09,040
to buy ingredients
and start selling food again.

171
00:14:10,200 --> 00:14:13,600
But those men might come back.

172
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:16,040
You should move somewhere else.

173
00:14:17,080 --> 00:14:19,240
Where am I supposed to go?

174
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:21,080
I've spent my whole life

175
00:14:21,160 --> 00:14:23,280
moving from place to place. I'm tired.

176
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:25,920
I don't have that many years left anyway.

177
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:28,680
If I'm going to die,
I might as well die here.

178
00:14:29,280 --> 00:14:33,160
Then I'll take you
to file a police report.

179
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:36,920
At least the police
can keep an eye on things.

180
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:39,400
All right.

181
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:50,480
I'll help you, Grandma.

182
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:54,720
I'll help.

183
00:15:05,920 --> 00:15:06,960
Here, Grandma.

184
00:15:08,080 --> 00:15:11,360
Use this as capital for your stall
so you don't have to borrow.

185
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:12,280
DUANGJAI'S FOOD STALL

186
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:15,960
I can't accept this. You've already
gotten into enough trouble because of me.

187
00:15:18,120 --> 00:15:19,120
Grandma,

188
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:24,280
you just taught
your granddaughter about gratitude.

189
00:15:24,800 --> 00:15:26,480
My own grandma died when I was little.

190
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:31,160
If you don't mind,
could you treat me like your grandson?

191
00:15:31,680 --> 00:15:33,120
I'll take care of you.

192
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:40,480
Please, Grandma. Take it.

193
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:41,920
Please.

194
00:15:48,880 --> 00:15:50,680
May you prosper

195
00:15:50,760 --> 00:15:53,080
and encounter only good things in life.

196
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:58,200
And may all the merit from your kindness
go to your parents

197
00:15:58,280 --> 00:16:00,360
for raising such a good man.

198
00:16:04,240 --> 00:16:05,200
Thank you.

199
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:09,160
I should get going.

200
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:11,360
Take good care of yourself,

201
00:16:11,440 --> 00:16:13,840
and wait for your granddaughter
to come home.

202
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:16,000
All right.

203
00:16:17,360 --> 00:16:21,480
Wait. I still don't know your name.

204
00:16:22,280 --> 00:16:23,280
Um...

205
00:16:24,200 --> 00:16:25,160
You can call me...

206
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:29,200
Weir.

207
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:34,440
If you're ever around here again,

208
00:16:34,520 --> 00:16:37,800
come visit me, Weir.

209
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:50,320
Dad.

210
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:53,280
Have you seen the video?

211
00:16:53,360 --> 00:16:56,000
What video?
I don't watch pointless nonsense.

212
00:16:58,080 --> 00:17:00,080
That video of the villagers
getting evicted.

213
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:04,079
- Boss, look at this.
<i>- I agree</i>

214
00:17:04,160 --> 00:17:06,000
<i>with development
and the greater good,</i>

215
00:17:06,599 --> 00:17:10,640
<i>but I don't agree with using the majority
as an excuse to ignore the minority.</i>

216
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:12,760
<i>True democracy isn't just</i>

217
00:17:12,839 --> 00:17:16,560
<i>about listening to the majority.
It also means listening to the minority.</i>

218
00:17:16,640 --> 00:17:20,720
<i>The majority should not be used
to pressure the minority.</i>

219
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:24,680
<i>We need to work together to solve this.
We need to find the fairest solution</i>

220
00:17:24,760 --> 00:17:26,000
<i>and proceed.</i>

221
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:31,680
Miss Hathaya!

222
00:17:31,760 --> 00:17:33,840
You've become famous.

223
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:37,000
Look! It's almost at a million views.

224
00:17:37,080 --> 00:17:38,720
What is it, Aunt Ann?

225
00:17:39,320 --> 00:17:43,320
Here. It's the video of you standing up
for the villagers facing demolition.

226
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:46,080
This is work time.

227
00:17:46,160 --> 00:17:48,240
Not time to sit around
watching pointless videos.

228
00:17:49,640 --> 00:17:53,240
Chamoi, when you spend hours
scrolling through videos,

229
00:17:53,320 --> 00:17:54,600
I never say anything.

230
00:17:54,680 --> 00:17:57,080
You're even more ridiculous than I am.

231
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:02,080
Look, Miss Hathaya.

232
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:04,760
Pathetic.

233
00:18:04,840 --> 00:18:08,920
Acting like some angel who helps everyone.

234
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:11,840
I know you filmed and edited this yourself

235
00:18:11,920 --> 00:18:15,640
because you wanted to get famous online.

236
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:16,760
Attention seeker!

237
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:19,120
I don't even have these clips,

238
00:18:19,200 --> 00:18:21,200
and I didn't film them myself.

239
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:24,000
It was probably one of the villagers
I helped who posted them.

240
00:18:24,560 --> 00:18:27,440
Miss Hathaya, look!
The views are shooting up!

241
00:18:27,520 --> 00:18:30,520
Hey! This is work time.

242
00:18:31,040 --> 00:18:33,640
Anyone caught watching videos
is getting reported to Madam.

243
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:39,520
Madam!

244
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:41,680
Madam! Madam!

245
00:18:41,760 --> 00:18:43,640
Madam, Hathaya

246
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:45,040
has become a TikTok star!

247
00:18:45,120 --> 00:18:47,680
She's almost at a million views!

248
00:18:47,760 --> 00:18:50,080
Stop screaming. I know.
I'm watching it right now!

249
00:18:51,560 --> 00:18:54,040
- Madam! Madam!
- Chamoi.

250
00:18:54,120 --> 00:18:56,280
Say one more word

251
00:18:56,360 --> 00:18:57,800
and I'll slap you!

252
00:18:59,840 --> 00:19:01,280
Hathaya

253
00:19:01,360 --> 00:19:03,360
has become the villagers' little angel.

254
00:19:03,880 --> 00:19:05,800
Everything she does gets praised.

255
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:09,360
Chayanee, sweetheart,
you need to do something.

256
00:19:10,680 --> 00:19:13,880
Mom, don't waste your time
on these ridiculous clips.

257
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:16,640
She can be an angel to a bunch
of parasites all she wants.

258
00:19:16,720 --> 00:19:17,800
So what?

259
00:19:18,320 --> 00:19:21,800
Her life will never be better than mine.

260
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:27,160
Where are you going?

261
00:19:27,960 --> 00:19:29,800
I have an important plan.

262
00:19:30,640 --> 00:19:32,080
With whom?

263
00:19:40,560 --> 00:19:42,920
Madam. Madam.

264
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:45,200
The shares... So many people shared this!

265
00:19:45,280 --> 00:19:47,360
- Chamoi!
- So many--

266
00:19:47,440 --> 00:19:48,480
Do you want to get fired?

267
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:50,960
Get out!

268
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:52,000
Yes Madam.

269
00:19:52,520 --> 00:19:54,640
My goodness.

270
00:19:58,560 --> 00:20:00,640
They posted that video
and made me look bad.

271
00:20:01,720 --> 00:20:02,960
I'll have someone

272
00:20:03,880 --> 00:20:04,960
burn their houses down.

273
00:20:06,040 --> 00:20:09,240
Dad, don't worry.

274
00:20:09,320 --> 00:20:10,520
The video they posted

275
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:12,960
only shows Hathaya asking for help
rehousing the villagers.

276
00:20:13,040 --> 00:20:16,120
They wouldn't dare upload
the part where they criticized you.

277
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:17,680
They know they were in the wrong too.

278
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:20,840
I'm going to have the officials
tear down all their houses.

279
00:20:20,920 --> 00:20:22,760
Then we'll build the road
for the public good.

280
00:20:23,760 --> 00:20:26,160
We need to score points
with people in the area.

281
00:20:26,960 --> 00:20:30,360
When you run in the next election,
they'll all vote for you.

282
00:20:32,080 --> 00:20:35,680
I think this is actually
a good opportunity to build support.

283
00:20:36,960 --> 00:20:38,280
What are you planning?

284
00:20:40,080 --> 00:20:42,160
Hathaya is trending right now.

285
00:20:43,160 --> 00:20:47,200
The media wants to cover her story.
If we use this opportunity,

286
00:20:47,280 --> 00:20:49,440
we can turn a crisis into an advantage.

287
00:20:57,480 --> 00:21:00,040
Everyone, let's work a little faster.

288
00:21:00,120 --> 00:21:02,200
The villagers will be able
to move in sooner.

289
00:21:02,280 --> 00:21:03,200
Yes!

290
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:13,800
Max, what are you doing?

291
00:21:15,320 --> 00:21:17,720
I want a selfie with a celebrity.

292
00:21:17,800 --> 00:21:19,160
You'll be unreachable soon.

293
00:21:19,240 --> 00:21:21,000
Get in.

294
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:24,000
Boss,

295
00:21:24,080 --> 00:21:25,600
- take one for me too.
- Aow,

296
00:21:26,600 --> 00:21:29,800
I think we should wait until break time.
The boss might yell at us.

297
00:21:29,880 --> 00:21:31,600
He's running an errand and won't be in.

298
00:21:31,680 --> 00:21:33,080
Well, what are we waiting for?

299
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:34,880
Come on! Come here!

300
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:36,640
Quickly.

301
00:21:40,160 --> 00:21:41,600
- Come on, guys!
- Let's go!

302
00:21:41,680 --> 00:21:44,120
Come on, everyone!
We're not leaving without a fight!

303
00:21:44,200 --> 00:21:45,480
Oh? Hey, hey.

304
00:21:46,240 --> 00:21:47,360
What happened now?

305
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:49,000
What's wrong?

306
00:21:49,640 --> 00:21:51,520
There's definitely a problem!
Right, everyone?

307
00:21:51,600 --> 00:21:53,280
- Yes!
- Wait.

308
00:21:53,360 --> 00:21:56,080
Everyone, calm down. What happened?

309
00:21:56,160 --> 00:21:59,720
Did they come to demolish your homes
and force you out today?

310
00:21:59,800 --> 00:22:01,280
No.

311
00:22:01,360 --> 00:22:06,200
The Subdistrict Office is giving us time
to finish the houses before we move.

312
00:22:06,280 --> 00:22:09,000
Then what's the problem?

313
00:22:09,080 --> 00:22:12,080
If you don't let us help
build our own homes,

314
00:22:12,160 --> 00:22:13,240
then we've got a problem!

315
00:22:13,320 --> 00:22:14,480
Right, everyone?

316
00:22:14,560 --> 00:22:16,480
- Yes!
- Yes!

317
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:20,400
Hathaya, you were kind enough
to help build housing for us,

318
00:22:20,480 --> 00:22:22,640
a roof over our heads.

319
00:22:22,720 --> 00:22:24,520
Please let us help build it too.

320
00:22:24,600 --> 00:22:27,720
Then what are we waiting for?
Let's build our homes together!

321
00:22:27,800 --> 00:22:28,760
Come on!

322
00:22:28,840 --> 00:22:30,520
- Let's do it!
- Let's do it!

323
00:22:30,600 --> 00:22:32,560
Let's go.

324
00:22:44,280 --> 00:22:47,480
Seeing everyone pitch in like this

325
00:22:47,560 --> 00:22:48,720
really warms my heart.

326
00:22:48,800 --> 00:22:50,240
Boss.

327
00:22:51,200 --> 00:22:52,040
Don't slack off.

328
00:22:52,120 --> 00:22:54,280
What, Aow? What did you say?

329
00:22:54,360 --> 00:22:57,320
Or I'll tell the boss.

330
00:22:58,160 --> 00:22:59,160
Are you threatening me?

331
00:22:59,240 --> 00:23:02,000
- Come here!
- No violence.

332
00:23:02,600 --> 00:23:06,040
Take this.

333
00:23:06,120 --> 00:23:07,280
No violence.

334
00:23:09,040 --> 00:23:10,080
Come here!

335
00:23:11,600 --> 00:23:14,080
Hathaya's mother gambled away
all her money

336
00:23:14,600 --> 00:23:15,600
and ran from her debts.

337
00:23:16,200 --> 00:23:18,560
Her grandmother really is sick.
She has heart disease.

338
00:23:19,200 --> 00:23:22,440
She earns money to support herself
and pay off debts while waiting

339
00:23:23,560 --> 00:23:25,040
for Hathaya to come home.

340
00:23:28,360 --> 00:23:29,440
Thank you.

341
00:23:30,240 --> 00:23:33,200
Everything Hathaya told you was true.

342
00:23:36,560 --> 00:23:39,480
Keep an eye on things for me.

343
00:23:40,400 --> 00:23:41,440
Yes, sir.

344
00:23:44,680 --> 00:23:48,800
Sir, have you seen Hathaya's video yet?

345
00:23:51,960 --> 00:23:53,040
May I?

346
00:24:00,440 --> 00:24:01,600
Mr. Saksit.

347
00:24:01,680 --> 00:24:03,240
Hello.

348
00:24:03,320 --> 00:24:04,400
Hello, Ms. Liu.

349
00:24:05,080 --> 00:24:07,160
What can we do for you?

350
00:24:07,240 --> 00:24:11,440
Or perhaps you'd like to buy
one or two houses?

351
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:14,960
For you, Mr. Saksit,
I can give you a special price.

352
00:24:16,320 --> 00:24:19,960
I'm here to see someone special.

353
00:24:21,440 --> 00:24:23,880
Oh, I'm so sorry.

354
00:24:23,960 --> 00:24:26,280
Chayanee isn't in the office today.

355
00:24:26,360 --> 00:24:30,040
I believe she went out to discuss
promoting the development.

356
00:24:31,640 --> 00:24:34,200
Actually, I'm not here to see Chayanee.

357
00:24:35,360 --> 00:24:37,640
Then who are you here to see?

358
00:24:37,720 --> 00:24:39,440
Dad is here to see Hathaya.

359
00:24:48,240 --> 00:24:49,440
Hathaya?

360
00:24:58,320 --> 00:24:59,440
Thank you.

361
00:25:00,120 --> 00:25:01,680
Do you remember me?

362
00:25:03,280 --> 00:25:04,320
Yes.

363
00:25:04,400 --> 00:25:07,440
I'm Raiwin, the Chief's son.
My father really wants to meet you.

364
00:25:11,600 --> 00:25:15,240
Hello, everyone! Hello!

365
00:25:15,320 --> 00:25:17,880
Reporters. These are

366
00:25:17,960 --> 00:25:20,760
residents from my subdistrict.

367
00:25:20,840 --> 00:25:22,200
Go ahead.

368
00:25:22,800 --> 00:25:26,320
I had a plan with Raiwin. He wouldn't
answer my calls, but now he's here?

369
00:25:26,400 --> 00:25:27,880
How could he do this?

370
00:25:28,680 --> 00:25:30,840
Chayanee, not yet.

371
00:25:31,840 --> 00:25:34,440
Everyone, the young woman standing here

372
00:25:34,520 --> 00:25:36,440
is Miss Hathaya.

373
00:25:37,040 --> 00:25:40,160
The villagers' angel
who has been helping local residents

374
00:25:40,240 --> 00:25:41,720
and is currently going viral online.

375
00:25:41,800 --> 00:25:44,080
Go ahead. Take pictures.

376
00:25:47,960 --> 00:25:49,960
And as

377
00:25:50,040 --> 00:25:51,600
the Subdistrict Chief here,

378
00:25:52,200 --> 00:25:55,320
I would like to sincerely
thank Miss Hathaya

379
00:25:55,400 --> 00:25:58,920
for her kindness in helping
these villagers find both housing

380
00:25:59,000 --> 00:26:00,480
and employment.

381
00:26:00,560 --> 00:26:03,520
I hope everyone here

382
00:26:03,600 --> 00:26:05,320
will look to Miss Hathaya

383
00:26:05,400 --> 00:26:08,800
as an example.
Let's give her another round of applause.

384
00:26:08,880 --> 00:26:10,160
Thank you.

385
00:26:12,400 --> 00:26:13,760
Father, did you stop by for work?

386
00:26:15,040 --> 00:26:18,280
Chayanee, take Grandpa into the office.

387
00:26:18,880 --> 00:26:22,000
No. I want to know what's happening.

388
00:26:22,840 --> 00:26:26,240
I'm Raiwin. I serve
as the Chief's assistant.

389
00:26:27,000 --> 00:26:29,200
On behalf of the Subdistrict Office,

390
00:26:29,720 --> 00:26:34,160
I'd like to present this gift basket
to Hathaya as a token of our appreciation.

391
00:26:34,240 --> 00:26:35,880
And I hope that in the future,

392
00:26:35,960 --> 00:26:37,800
we can continue working together

393
00:26:37,880 --> 00:26:40,160
to help improve our community.

394
00:26:43,400 --> 00:26:44,440
Okay.

395
00:26:44,520 --> 00:26:46,560
Pictures! Stand closer together.

396
00:26:47,160 --> 00:26:49,360
This is my son.
He's pleased to meet you all.

397
00:26:49,440 --> 00:26:52,160
- Please look at this camera.
- Take pictures.

398
00:26:52,240 --> 00:26:53,600
Yes.

399
00:26:54,760 --> 00:26:56,960
You can interview her now.

400
00:26:57,040 --> 00:26:59,800
- Go ahead and interview Miss Hathaya.
- Thank you.

401
00:26:59,880 --> 00:27:01,080
You can interview her now.

402
00:27:05,280 --> 00:27:08,080
People online have been
praising you as an angel

403
00:27:08,160 --> 00:27:12,000
because of your kindness.
Why did you decide to help the villagers?

404
00:27:12,080 --> 00:27:14,600
That's right. These days, so many people

405
00:27:14,680 --> 00:27:16,880
only think about themselves.

406
00:27:16,960 --> 00:27:19,680
Why did you choose to help them?

407
00:27:20,520 --> 00:27:21,520
She's stupid.

408
00:27:21,600 --> 00:27:24,760
She won't know what to say.
Let her embarrass herself at the mic.

409
00:27:25,360 --> 00:27:28,680
First, I'd like to correct one thing.

410
00:27:29,240 --> 00:27:30,720
I'm not an angel.

411
00:27:30,800 --> 00:27:34,320
I'm just an ordinary person
like everyone else.

412
00:27:34,400 --> 00:27:37,120
If you ask why I decided to help...

413
00:27:38,120 --> 00:27:40,280
I've struggled in life too.

414
00:27:40,360 --> 00:27:41,800
That's why I understand them.

415
00:27:44,960 --> 00:27:47,640
I simply wanted to solve
the problem in front of me

416
00:27:47,720 --> 00:27:50,000
and find the best possible solution
for everyone.

417
00:27:50,080 --> 00:27:51,400
How do you feel about

418
00:27:51,480 --> 00:27:53,600
the villagers and people online

419
00:27:53,680 --> 00:27:55,720
calling you an angel?

420
00:27:55,800 --> 00:27:58,640
I'm very grateful for every comment,

421
00:27:58,720 --> 00:28:01,920
but I really can't take the credit

422
00:28:02,000 --> 00:28:05,280
because none of my ideas
would have happened

423
00:28:05,360 --> 00:28:09,400
without the approval of Mr. Pichai,
the owner of this project.

424
00:28:10,200 --> 00:28:12,280
Mr. Pichai provided the land

425
00:28:12,360 --> 00:28:14,840
where the villagers
can stay and work here.

426
00:28:14,920 --> 00:28:17,640
He helped them without
expecting anything in return.

427
00:28:17,720 --> 00:28:21,200
The housing development
he created has a slogan,

428
00:28:21,280 --> 00:28:23,080
"The Family."

429
00:28:23,160 --> 00:28:25,640
Family means helping one another.

430
00:28:25,720 --> 00:28:29,720
And his idea of family doesn't mean
only a father, mother, and children.

431
00:28:29,800 --> 00:28:31,960
Our family is bigger than that.

432
00:28:32,040 --> 00:28:35,120
We are a community.
We are a society that helps one another.

433
00:28:36,280 --> 00:28:39,400
If you reporters would like more details,

434
00:28:40,120 --> 00:28:42,280
you can interview him directly.

435
00:28:42,800 --> 00:28:45,400
- May I?
- There he is.

436
00:28:50,520 --> 00:28:52,560
Sir, may we interview you?

437
00:28:53,160 --> 00:28:54,680
Of course.

438
00:28:54,760 --> 00:28:56,520
How long will you allow them to stay here?

439
00:28:56,600 --> 00:28:57,640
Well...

440
00:29:01,520 --> 00:29:03,200
Excuse me. I need to get back to work.

441
00:29:03,280 --> 00:29:04,320
Of course.

442
00:29:19,360 --> 00:29:21,800
Max, share the fruit with everyone.

443
00:29:22,600 --> 00:29:24,800
The Chief gave it to you.
You should keep it.

444
00:29:24,880 --> 00:29:26,280
You don't want any?

445
00:29:27,320 --> 00:29:28,960
It's expensive stuff.

446
00:29:29,040 --> 00:29:31,080
Of course I want some. Looks delicious!

447
00:29:31,160 --> 00:29:32,240
Thank you!

448
00:29:32,320 --> 00:29:33,880
Okay.

449
00:29:33,960 --> 00:29:36,000
- Make sure you share.
- I'm not sharing!

450
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:43,280
Very impressive.

451
00:29:43,360 --> 00:29:45,280
Where did you study acting?

452
00:29:45,360 --> 00:29:47,920
You sure know how to put on a show
and talk a good game.

453
00:29:48,520 --> 00:29:49,600
Flawless performance.

454
00:29:49,680 --> 00:29:51,080
If you just came to be sarcastic,

455
00:29:51,160 --> 00:29:53,320
excuse me. I have work to do.

456
00:29:54,480 --> 00:29:55,360
Wait!

457
00:29:55,440 --> 00:29:56,960
What?

458
00:30:01,320 --> 00:30:04,960
I wanted to thank you
on behalf of the villagers.

459
00:30:08,480 --> 00:30:11,080
That sounds really strange
coming from you.

460
00:30:11,800 --> 00:30:14,000
Then get back to work.

461
00:30:14,520 --> 00:30:17,920
Don't think being a good person
means you can slack off. Go!

462
00:30:19,640 --> 00:30:22,840
Now that sounds like the real Ramil.

463
00:30:22,920 --> 00:30:24,040
Much more familiar.

464
00:30:46,200 --> 00:30:48,120
Why did you come see me?

465
00:30:49,320 --> 00:30:53,160
If you're so impressed
with Hathaya, then go see her.

466
00:30:56,400 --> 00:30:58,360
I don't have feelings for your cousin.

467
00:31:00,400 --> 00:31:04,160
If you don't, then why are you
getting involved with her?

468
00:31:06,440 --> 00:31:07,880
I hate her.

469
00:31:09,560 --> 00:31:13,280
Dad wants me to run in the next election.

470
00:31:13,880 --> 00:31:16,920
So we need to ride Hathaya's popularity
to build support.

471
00:31:24,520 --> 00:31:25,440
Hey.

472
00:31:28,080 --> 00:31:29,560
You're the only one I have.

473
00:31:40,840 --> 00:31:43,760
I need to be
the most important woman in your life.

474
00:31:44,520 --> 00:31:46,680
And the only one.

475
00:31:55,040 --> 00:31:57,080
I'm not going to ask you
to believe my words.

476
00:31:58,680 --> 00:32:02,520
I'll show you how much I love you.

477
00:32:15,040 --> 00:32:17,560
Come on in.

478
00:32:18,160 --> 00:32:19,200
You can come inside now.

479
00:32:19,280 --> 00:32:20,360
Let's go.

480
00:32:20,440 --> 00:32:21,440
Come on.

481
00:32:21,520 --> 00:32:24,000
- Go. Come on in.
- Let's go.

482
00:32:27,120 --> 00:32:28,840
Come on, guys.

483
00:32:30,080 --> 00:32:31,400
Wow.

484
00:32:32,320 --> 00:32:33,440
- So cute.
- Coming through.

485
00:32:34,400 --> 00:32:36,680
- Nice work, Max.
- Let's go.

486
00:32:54,480 --> 00:32:56,360
This is your place now.

487
00:32:57,200 --> 00:32:59,160
No one is going to force you out again.

488
00:33:00,480 --> 00:33:02,200
We have a place to live now, everyone!

489
00:33:02,280 --> 00:33:03,760
Give yourselves a big hand!

490
00:33:05,560 --> 00:33:07,840
I'm so happy.

491
00:33:07,920 --> 00:33:10,640
We don't have to live
on the street anymore.

492
00:33:11,160 --> 00:33:12,200
Aw.

493
00:33:13,200 --> 00:33:15,760
No more homeless life.

494
00:33:16,360 --> 00:33:18,000
Thank you so much.

495
00:33:18,080 --> 00:33:20,120
Put the eggs right here.

496
00:33:20,200 --> 00:33:21,760
Thank you.

497
00:33:21,840 --> 00:33:23,680
Please put it there.

498
00:33:23,760 --> 00:33:25,600
- Alright.
- This can go there.

499
00:33:25,680 --> 00:33:28,720
Thank you very much.

500
00:33:28,800 --> 00:33:29,880
Oh.

501
00:33:41,160 --> 00:33:43,640
Please let us live here
in peace and happiness.

502
00:33:44,280 --> 00:33:46,400
<i>Sadhu.</i>

503
00:33:54,960 --> 00:33:57,600
And may our angel protect us too.

504
00:34:03,480 --> 00:34:05,520
Something delicious.

505
00:34:05,600 --> 00:34:07,120
- What do you want?
- Frog?

506
00:34:07,200 --> 00:34:09,080
Bullfrog?

507
00:34:12,480 --> 00:34:16,760
All homeowners, please come
over here for a group photo!

508
00:34:16,840 --> 00:34:18,280
- Come on.
- Everyone.

509
00:34:18,360 --> 00:34:20,239
Come on.

510
00:34:20,320 --> 00:34:22,080
Come on.

511
00:34:23,280 --> 00:34:24,480
Now.

512
00:34:24,560 --> 00:34:26,480
Come in.

513
00:34:26,560 --> 00:34:28,920
- One--
- Wait!

514
00:34:29,440 --> 00:34:31,040
Come take the picture with us.

515
00:34:31,120 --> 00:34:33,040
- It's okay.
- Come on.

516
00:34:33,120 --> 00:34:34,520
- Come in.
- No.

517
00:34:34,600 --> 00:34:35,520
Let's take picture.

518
00:34:35,600 --> 00:34:37,480
- Come on.
- You helped build this house for me.

519
00:34:37,560 --> 00:34:38,920
That makes this your home too.

520
00:34:39,000 --> 00:34:40,600
Yes.

521
00:34:40,679 --> 00:34:42,960
All right, ready?

522
00:34:43,040 --> 00:34:45,159
One, two, three!

523
00:34:46,000 --> 00:34:48,800
Okay, one more! One, two, three!

524
00:34:48,880 --> 00:34:51,960
Smile! One, two, three!

525
00:34:52,040 --> 00:34:53,840
Wait!

526
00:34:53,920 --> 00:34:55,040
Hey, come join us.

527
00:34:56,600 --> 00:35:00,520
No. I'm busy. I have to get back to work.

528
00:35:01,120 --> 00:35:04,800
Everyone, there's one
very important person we can't forget.

529
00:35:04,880 --> 00:35:05,720
Ramil.

530
00:35:06,640 --> 00:35:08,360
A round of applause, please.

531
00:35:08,440 --> 00:35:10,120
Yeah!

532
00:35:11,200 --> 00:35:13,840
Ramil supervised all of the construction.

533
00:35:13,920 --> 00:35:16,680
And he'll also be the supervisor
taking care of all of us.

534
00:35:16,760 --> 00:35:19,080
Boss, please look after us.

535
00:35:19,160 --> 00:35:22,280
Please take care of us.

536
00:35:23,160 --> 00:35:24,360
Make yourselves at home.

537
00:35:24,440 --> 00:35:26,520
Where are you going?

538
00:35:26,600 --> 00:35:28,400
To work.

539
00:35:29,680 --> 00:35:31,720
You have to welcome the new members first.

540
00:35:33,640 --> 00:35:35,200
No. I don't know what to say.

541
00:35:35,280 --> 00:35:38,600
My boss isn't very good at talking,
but he's a great dancer!

542
00:35:38,680 --> 00:35:40,400
- Huh?
- Really?

543
00:35:40,480 --> 00:35:42,200
Then...

544
00:35:42,280 --> 00:35:45,040
Show us some moves, boss!

545
00:35:45,120 --> 00:35:46,600
No way!

546
00:36:00,040 --> 00:36:01,080
That's enough.

547
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:04,360
Pictures!

548
00:36:04,440 --> 00:36:06,920
- Come on.
- Come on.

549
00:36:07,000 --> 00:36:08,240
Come on.

550
00:36:08,320 --> 00:36:09,880
Let's take pictures.

551
00:36:10,880 --> 00:36:13,040
Come here. One, two, three!

552
00:36:24,440 --> 00:36:26,920
Hey! Where are you going?

553
00:36:27,520 --> 00:36:28,840
To work.

554
00:36:29,360 --> 00:36:32,240
And don't ever do that again.

555
00:36:32,840 --> 00:36:35,280
Do what?

556
00:36:35,360 --> 00:36:38,640
Well, making me dance.

557
00:36:39,800 --> 00:36:41,040
Why?

558
00:36:41,680 --> 00:36:42,720
It was cute.

559
00:36:43,320 --> 00:36:46,520
No. I was embarrassed.

560
00:36:48,360 --> 00:36:52,160
Okay. I won't do it again.

561
00:37:02,960 --> 00:37:04,640
Why do you go this far for people?

562
00:37:09,160 --> 00:37:10,640
MODERN SINGLE-STORY HOME DEVELOPMENT

563
00:37:14,120 --> 00:37:17,200
The model home is finished, and the first
phase of the development is ready.

564
00:37:17,280 --> 00:37:22,040
I want to launch the campaign. We'll hire
a famous actor for a photoshoot.

565
00:37:23,680 --> 00:37:25,440
These days,

566
00:37:25,960 --> 00:37:28,240
I think we should find newer ways

567
00:37:28,800 --> 00:37:31,680
to reach customers directly.
Wouldn't that be better?

568
00:37:31,760 --> 00:37:33,440
Father,

569
00:37:33,520 --> 00:37:35,880
Chayanee has thought
this through carefully.

570
00:37:35,960 --> 00:37:38,640
These days, people love celebrities

571
00:37:38,720 --> 00:37:41,200
and want to copy everything they do.

572
00:37:41,280 --> 00:37:44,440
That's true. I follow celebrities too.

573
00:37:44,520 --> 00:37:47,960
When I see what they eat or buy,
I want it too.

574
00:37:53,080 --> 00:37:55,160
Grandpa.

575
00:37:57,360 --> 00:37:59,000
Please sign it.

576
00:38:00,040 --> 00:38:02,160
Then I can start today.

577
00:38:09,920 --> 00:38:12,760
Sir, there are a lot of customers
at the model home.

578
00:38:22,240 --> 00:38:24,120
Father, look.

579
00:38:24,200 --> 00:38:25,800
Chayanee hasn't even started her campaign,

580
00:38:25,880 --> 00:38:27,720
and it's already bringing us good luck.

581
00:38:28,720 --> 00:38:31,120
Customers are pouring in
to reserve houses.

582
00:38:31,200 --> 00:38:33,200
Once I finish the PR campaign,

583
00:38:33,280 --> 00:38:35,360
the first phase
will probably sell out instantly.

584
00:38:38,960 --> 00:38:40,120
Oh.

585
00:38:40,680 --> 00:38:42,600
- Hello.
- Hello.

586
00:38:42,680 --> 00:38:44,480
I saw your interview the other day.

587
00:38:44,560 --> 00:38:46,480
My wife and I became
interested in this place.

588
00:38:46,560 --> 00:38:49,680
To be honest, we were hesitant at first.

589
00:38:49,760 --> 00:38:51,400
Housing developments are all the same.

590
00:38:51,480 --> 00:38:54,040
But we came
because I liked your philosophy

591
00:38:54,120 --> 00:38:55,760
to help people and give opportunities.

592
00:38:55,840 --> 00:38:59,840
Thank you for placing your trust in us.

593
00:39:00,360 --> 00:39:03,080
I assure you that every home
is built to a high standard.

594
00:39:03,160 --> 00:39:06,320
And we'll take care of you after the sale
as if you were part of our family.

595
00:39:07,320 --> 00:39:10,400
Then there's nothing left to think about.
I'll put down a deposit today.

596
00:39:12,080 --> 00:39:14,120
Where's the worker named Hathaya?

597
00:39:15,120 --> 00:39:16,200
Why?

598
00:39:16,280 --> 00:39:19,800
Did Hathaya cause
some kind of problem for you?

599
00:39:19,880 --> 00:39:20,760
Oh no!

600
00:39:20,840 --> 00:39:23,080
We sincerely apologize.

601
00:39:23,160 --> 00:39:26,080
That worker is always causing trouble.

602
00:39:44,360 --> 00:39:47,000
Grandpa, why did you call me here?

603
00:39:47,520 --> 00:39:51,760
Did I do something wrong?

604
00:39:53,840 --> 00:39:55,400
Hathaya,

605
00:39:55,480 --> 00:39:57,840
you're even prettier in person
than you are in the video.

606
00:39:57,920 --> 00:40:00,880
My boyfriend hardly
ever shares anything online,

607
00:40:00,960 --> 00:40:04,760
but he liked and shared
your video with all his friends.

608
00:40:04,840 --> 00:40:06,000
I like the way you think.

609
00:40:06,080 --> 00:40:08,920
You said what people
all over Thailand are feeling.

610
00:40:09,560 --> 00:40:12,680
Officials need to take a hard look
at how they do their jobs too.

611
00:40:12,760 --> 00:40:14,800
I cried when I watched your video.

612
00:40:14,880 --> 00:40:17,080
My life wasn't that different from theirs.

613
00:40:17,160 --> 00:40:19,000
I only have what I have today

614
00:40:19,080 --> 00:40:21,320
because someone gave me an opportunity.

615
00:40:21,400 --> 00:40:24,480
Thank you. And thank you
on their behalf too.

616
00:40:24,560 --> 00:40:26,600
You don't need to thank me.

617
00:40:27,360 --> 00:40:28,440
You should thank Mr. Pichai.

618
00:40:29,560 --> 00:40:32,480
He is always willing to give people
opportunities and support them.

619
00:40:32,560 --> 00:40:35,880
We decided to buy here
because of your kindness

620
00:40:36,400 --> 00:40:38,520
and Mr. Pichai's values.

621
00:40:40,480 --> 00:40:43,400
I believe that when workers
put their hearts into what they do,

622
00:40:43,480 --> 00:40:46,400
the houses they build will turn out well.
They'll become perfect homes.

623
00:40:47,000 --> 00:40:49,640
I'm going to promote
this development to my friends

624
00:40:49,720 --> 00:40:51,760
and everyone I know.

625
00:40:51,840 --> 00:40:54,160
I won't charge you
a single baht in commission.

626
00:40:55,080 --> 00:40:57,720
Thank you so much. Thank you very much.

627
00:40:58,520 --> 00:41:00,000
Thank you very much.

628
00:41:02,800 --> 00:41:04,560
Stop filming! Let's go!

629
00:41:06,000 --> 00:41:07,160
Thank you.

630
00:41:10,920 --> 00:41:13,280
You're adorable.

631
00:41:13,360 --> 00:41:14,720
So happy to meet you.

632
00:41:14,800 --> 00:41:18,240
After the customers leave,
bring Hathaya to see me in the office.

633
00:41:18,840 --> 00:41:19,880
Yes, sir.

634
00:41:20,400 --> 00:41:21,320
Thank you.

635
00:41:27,400 --> 00:41:28,240
MODERN SINGLE-STORY HOME DEVELOPMENT

636
00:41:28,320 --> 00:41:30,320
ONLY FIVE UNITS REMAINING

637
00:41:30,400 --> 00:41:32,680
I've already spoken to the actor.

638
00:41:32,760 --> 00:41:34,560
Grandpa, please approve the budget,

639
00:41:34,640 --> 00:41:36,760
then I'll bring him in
for the photoshoot right away.

640
00:41:38,560 --> 00:41:40,440
Please, Father.

641
00:41:43,360 --> 00:41:46,600
Grandpa, did you want to see me?

642
00:41:47,200 --> 00:41:49,960
After today, you don't have
to work on site anymore.

643
00:41:53,200 --> 00:41:55,200
You're sending Hathaya home, right?

644
00:41:56,280 --> 00:41:59,200
Probably for the best.
She's done nothing but cause trouble.

645
00:42:00,240 --> 00:42:03,040
So go back to your life
in the countryside.

646
00:42:03,720 --> 00:42:06,200
I'm bringing Hathaya into the office
to help with the work.

647
00:42:13,000 --> 00:42:16,600
Grandpa, do you mean you want Hathaya
to make copies and deliver documents?

648
00:42:16,680 --> 00:42:18,920
I want Hathaya to be your assistant.

649
00:42:19,440 --> 00:42:21,440
You two will work together
on promoting the project.

650
00:42:25,400 --> 00:42:27,520
This plan costs more than necessary.

651
00:42:28,120 --> 00:42:31,480
We can already reach customers
directly through social media.

652
00:42:32,000 --> 00:42:35,440
And Hathaya has already
laid the groundwork.

653
00:42:36,040 --> 00:42:39,280
Build on what you've already started
and come up with a PR plan.

654
00:42:40,920 --> 00:42:42,200
Yes, Grandpa.

655
00:42:43,800 --> 00:42:46,960
Father, these houses cost millions.

656
00:42:47,040 --> 00:42:49,440
Using only social media advertising

657
00:42:49,520 --> 00:42:51,320
makes the project look cheap.

658
00:42:52,400 --> 00:42:55,280
Today's reservations already proved

659
00:42:55,840 --> 00:42:58,000
that we don't need to spend
that much money.

660
00:42:59,360 --> 00:43:02,000
Marketing based on trust

661
00:43:02,080 --> 00:43:04,040
and sincerity is important too.

662
00:43:04,640 --> 00:43:09,440
And if you really think
the project needs a spokesperson,

663
00:43:10,840 --> 00:43:13,040
Hathaya would be the right person for it.

664
00:43:24,720 --> 00:43:26,520
I agree with Grandpa.

665
00:43:27,920 --> 00:43:30,840
Maybe we should try something new.

666
00:43:31,800 --> 00:43:34,760
I believe Hathaya will do a great job.

667
00:43:36,640 --> 00:43:38,920
Let's work together.

668
00:43:42,000 --> 00:43:44,480
Of course. I'll do my very best.

669
00:43:49,440 --> 00:43:51,640
I'll give it everything I have, Grandpa.

670
00:43:53,400 --> 00:43:56,640
Ramil, I want you
to speed up the construction.

671
00:43:57,200 --> 00:43:59,720
I believe sales are going
to increase after this.

672
00:44:01,320 --> 00:44:02,320
Yes, sir.

673
00:44:12,880 --> 00:44:15,880
Whoa. Hey.

674
00:44:17,480 --> 00:44:20,640
What happened? Calm down.

675
00:44:21,280 --> 00:44:23,680
Grandpa is letting Hathaya
work in marketing.

676
00:44:23,760 --> 00:44:26,240
Soon I'll be reporting to her.

677
00:44:29,320 --> 00:44:33,040
Your cousin is... pretty capable.

678
00:44:35,400 --> 00:44:37,720
She'll probably be
a big help to your grandpa.

679
00:44:38,320 --> 00:44:40,680
So now you think
she's better than me too?!

680
00:44:41,720 --> 00:44:44,240
That's not what I mean.
Those are two different things.

681
00:44:45,040 --> 00:44:47,560
Calm down. Sit.

682
00:44:51,920 --> 00:44:56,440
Instead of getting angry, you should
be happy someone is coming to help.

683
00:44:56,520 --> 00:45:00,760
Your grandpa will still
put you in charge of her.

684
00:45:04,080 --> 00:45:05,720
You're right.

685
00:45:07,280 --> 00:45:11,400
Raiwin, I want you to make
our relationship public to Grandpa.

686
00:45:11,920 --> 00:45:15,760
I think the sooner we get married,

687
00:45:15,840 --> 00:45:19,120
the sooner Grandpa
might hand the business over to us.

688
00:45:22,720 --> 00:45:24,720
You think much further ahead than I do.

689
00:45:26,040 --> 00:45:27,440
You're amazing.

690
00:45:29,280 --> 00:45:31,200
I have to do everything I can

691
00:45:32,480 --> 00:45:34,080
before Hathaya

692
00:45:34,600 --> 00:45:36,480
steals what belongs to me.

693
00:45:39,400 --> 00:45:42,120
- <i>Okay.</i>
- <i>Give her a big hand!</i>

694
00:45:44,640 --> 00:45:47,280
<i>One, two, three! Yeah!</i>

695
00:45:52,440 --> 00:45:53,280
Dad,

696
00:45:53,880 --> 00:45:56,560
there's something important
I need to talk to you about.

697
00:45:56,640 --> 00:45:59,080
I have something to discuss with you too.

698
00:45:59,840 --> 00:46:01,120
You go first.

699
00:46:01,200 --> 00:46:04,760
You already know Chayanee and I have been

700
00:46:04,840 --> 00:46:06,600
seeing each other for a while, right?

701
00:46:08,720 --> 00:46:09,560
So?

702
00:46:10,400 --> 00:46:13,480
Mr. Pichai is very protective
of his granddaughter.

703
00:46:15,280 --> 00:46:19,280
I'd like you to talk to him

704
00:46:19,360 --> 00:46:22,560
and ask for his permission for me
to seriously date Chayanee.

705
00:46:23,160 --> 00:46:25,680
Mr. Pichai's granddaughter?

706
00:46:29,560 --> 00:46:31,840
That family is worth hundreds of millions.

707
00:46:33,920 --> 00:46:37,280
And since we're in politics, it benefits
us to have connections in construction.

708
00:46:40,480 --> 00:46:44,840
It'll keep the wealth in the family.

709
00:47:00,960 --> 00:47:04,240
A construction foreman like you
belongs at the work site.

710
00:47:05,600 --> 00:47:09,080
A respectable mansion like this isn't
a place for someone as low-class as you.

711
00:47:16,080 --> 00:47:17,720
Thank you for the advice.

712
00:47:19,040 --> 00:47:22,160
And where should someone like you be?

713
00:47:22,240 --> 00:47:24,040
Don't get smart with me.

714
00:47:24,120 --> 00:47:28,240
You're the Chief.
You should be at the Subdistrict Office.

715
00:47:28,880 --> 00:47:32,160
Do your job and make your salary
worth the taxpayers' money.

716
00:47:32,240 --> 00:47:34,840
Don't go around courting businesspeople

717
00:47:34,920 --> 00:47:36,280
for your own benefit.

718
00:47:36,360 --> 00:47:37,960
- Ramil!
- What are you doing here?

719
00:47:40,480 --> 00:47:41,840
I'm picking Hathaya up for work.

720
00:47:42,480 --> 00:47:46,640
Dad and I have an appointment
with Mr. Pichai. We called ahead.

721
00:47:47,160 --> 00:47:49,560
Dad, I'll go get the gift basket.

722
00:47:49,640 --> 00:47:50,640
No.

723
00:47:52,680 --> 00:47:53,640
You.

724
00:47:54,600 --> 00:47:56,560
Go get the flower basket
from the car for me.

725
00:48:00,720 --> 00:48:02,640
Didn't you hear what I said?

726
00:48:03,600 --> 00:48:07,000
At least, you should remember everything
I did for you when I raised you.

727
00:48:08,440 --> 00:48:09,480
Go.

728
00:48:15,000 --> 00:48:16,080
Yes, sir.

729
00:48:29,160 --> 00:48:30,640
Chayanee, sweetheart.

730
00:48:30,720 --> 00:48:32,840
Raiwin brought Mr. Saksit.
They're already here.

731
00:48:34,240 --> 00:48:35,920
Mom, go and welcome the guests.

732
00:48:36,000 --> 00:48:37,640
I just need to touch up a little more.

733
00:48:38,880 --> 00:48:40,600
I'm so excited.

734
00:48:40,680 --> 00:48:43,240
My lady is finally going
to introduce her husband.

735
00:48:44,200 --> 00:48:45,040
- Chamoi!
- Yes?

736
00:48:45,920 --> 00:48:49,240
That's inappropriate.
She's just introducing her boyfriend.

737
00:48:51,040 --> 00:48:51,880
Yes. Boyfriend.

738
00:48:51,960 --> 00:48:53,920
Go downstairs and take care of the guests!

739
00:48:55,400 --> 00:48:56,720
Yes, ma'am.

740
00:48:59,800 --> 00:49:00,640
Hurry up, sweetheart.

741
00:49:01,640 --> 00:49:02,760
Okay.

742
00:49:09,080 --> 00:49:11,600
Mr. Saksit, is there something
you wanted to discuss?

743
00:49:14,120 --> 00:49:16,840
I'll get straight to the point.

744
00:49:18,920 --> 00:49:21,120
My son Raiwin

745
00:49:21,200 --> 00:49:23,360
has feelings for your granddaughter.

746
00:49:25,080 --> 00:49:28,040
He asked me to come and ask you

747
00:49:28,120 --> 00:49:30,000
for permission
so they can do this properly.

748
00:49:30,080 --> 00:49:33,280
I understand that love and attraction
are personal matters.

749
00:49:34,240 --> 00:49:37,640
But I admire young people who show respect

750
00:49:38,440 --> 00:49:40,000
to the woman's elders.

751
00:49:40,640 --> 00:49:41,560
Raiwin.

752
00:49:44,720 --> 00:49:46,480
Thank you, Mr. Pichai.

753
00:49:52,880 --> 00:49:53,960
I...

754
00:49:55,040 --> 00:49:59,560
I would like to ask
your permission to date Hathaya.

755
00:50:13,400 --> 00:50:16,560
<i>And now she's trying
to steal the man I love.</i>

756
00:50:17,080 --> 00:50:20,920
NEXT EPISODE

757
00:50:21,000 --> 00:50:22,720
<i>I hate her.</i>

758
00:50:23,760 --> 00:50:27,440
Watch yourself. Your little sister
might not be too happy.

759
00:50:27,520 --> 00:50:30,000
<i>I'll get Pong
to drag her straight to hell.</i>

760
00:51:29,880 --> 00:51:30,760
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
